   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">The exploratory IRT model will always fit better than a confirmatory one in terms of log-likelihood criteria (it is a highly over-parameterized model). Regarding your questions<div><br></div><div>1. If you translate this into a type of Q-matrix and pass that to mirt.model() then you could get this structure automatically.</div><div><br></div><div>2. Not that I can see. F2 might be a little under-defined empirically, but it could be fine if the correlations between the auxillary traits is reasonably high (that would help with stability). <br><div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Phil</div></div></div></div><br></div></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
